FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Senior Executive Service. The ranges of rates of basic pay for senior\nexecutives in the Senior Executive Service, as established pursuant to 5\nU.S.C. 5382, as amended by section 1125 of Public Law 108–136, are set\nforth on Schedule 4 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"69 FR 10891 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 2","sha256":"e06338b7a37ec628875ae7835af2677fddc0347265ebf21ec6cce7a3e11be9ee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Executive and Certain Other Salaries. The rates of basic pay or\nsalaries for the following offices and positions are set forth on the schedules\nattached hereto and made a part hereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"69 FR 10891 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"e06338b7a37ec628875ae7835af2677fddc0347265ebf21ec6cce7a3e11be9ee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Executive Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5311–5318) at Schedule 5;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"69 FR 10891 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"e06338b7a37ec628875ae7835af2677fddc0347265ebf21ec6cce7a3e11be9ee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Vice President (3 U.S.C. 104) and the Congress (2 U.S.C. 31)\nat Schedule 6; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"69 FR 10891 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"e06338b7a37ec628875ae7835af2677fddc0347265ebf21ec6cce7a3e11be9ee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Justices and judges (28 U.S.C. 5, 44(d), 135, 252, and 461(a), section\n140 of Public Law 97–92, and Public Law 108–167) at Schedule 7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"69 FR 10891 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"e06338b7a37ec628875ae7835af2677fddc0347265ebf21ec6cce7a3e11be9ee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Uniformed Services. Pursuant to section 601(a)–(b) of Public Law\n108–136, the rates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. 203) for members of\nthe uniformed services, as adjusted under 37 U.S.C. 1009, and the rate\nof monthly cadet or midshipman pay are set forth on Schedule 8 attached\nhereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"69 FR 10891 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 4","sha256":"e06338b7a37ec628875ae7835af2677fddc0347265ebf21ec6cce7a3e11be9ee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 5304 of title 5, United States Code, and in accord-\nance with section 640(a) of Division F of Public Law 108–199, locality-\nbased comparability payments shall be paid in accordance with Schedule\n9 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"69 FR 10891 (PDF p. 1); Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"e06338b7a37ec628875ae7835af2677fddc0347265ebf21ec6cce7a3e11be9ee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2004-03-08/pdf/04-5322.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13332#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predica